  "message": "Good question—on our side, I’ve already enabled roaming for your line, so your phone should now be allowed to use data abroad. If the Data Roaming switch on the phone won’t stay ON, it’s usually a device-side setting or a software quirk. Here’s the plan, in order, and why: Goal: get your phone off 2G and onto 4G/5G, remove bottlenecks (VPN), and ensure roaming is actually ON at the device level. Step 1 — Disconnect the VPN (common blocker) • Action: disconnect_vpn. • Reason: VPNs can prevent connections from establishing while roaming or make them appear as “no connection.” Step 2 — Try enabling Data Roaming again • Action: toggle_roaming (turn ON). • After toggling, wait ~10 seconds. • Tell me exactly what happens: is the switch greyed out, does it flip back to OFF, or does it stay ON but you still see 2G/no data? Step 3 — Prefer fast networks • Action: set_network_mode_preference to \"4g_5g_preferred\" (2G cannot deliver excellent speeds). Step 4 — Refresh the data session • Action: toggle_data OFF, wait 10 seconds, then toggle_data ON. Step 5 — Quick device refresh if needed • If the Data Roaming toggle still won’t stay ON: reboot_device, then try toggle_roaming again. Step 6 — SIM reseat (only if still stuck) • If it still won’t enable after reboot: reseat_sim_card, then try toggle_roaming again. Step 7 — Verify and test • Action: check_network_status and share: signal bars, network type (aiming for 4G/5G), and whether Data Roaming shows ON. • Then run_speed_test and share the result label. Extra checks: • If your phone is company-managed (work profile/MDM), roaming may be restricted. Let me know if it’s a work-managed device. Please start with Step 1 (disconnect VPN), then Step 2 (toggle Data Roaming ON) and tell me what exactly happens with the toggle. I’ll adjust immediately based on your result."
}

