messages.content:
{
  "message": "Great—roaming is now ON and VPN is OFF. You’re still on 2G with 1 bar, so the next priority is to get your phone to prefer 4G/5G and refresh the network registration. Here’s my plan and why: 2G cannot deliver excellent speeds. Forcing the device to prefer 4G/5G and refreshing the radio often bumps it to a faster local partner network when roaming. Please do these steps in order: Step 1 — Prefer 4G/5G • Action: check_network_mode_preference. If it’s set to 2G/3G or similar, set_network_mode_preference to \"4g_5g_preferred\". • Reason: Ensures the phone will try 4G/5G instead of sticking to 2G. Step 2 — Refresh the radio registration • Action: toggle_airplane_mode ON for 20 seconds, then OFF. • Reason: Forces the phone to drop the 2G cell and re-register, often landing on a faster network. Step 3 — Refresh the data session • Action: toggle_data OFF, wait 10 seconds, then toggle_data ON. Step 4 — Make sure nothing is throttling data locally • Action: check_data_restriction_status. If Data Saver is ON, toggle_data_saver_mode to turn it OFF. Step 5 — Verify and test • Action: check_network_status and tell me: • Bars • Network type (ideally 4G/LTE or 5G) • Data roaming shows ON? • Then run_speed_test and share the result label. If you’re still stuck on 2G after Step 5: Step 6 — Quick device refresh • Action: reboot_device, wait 1–2 minutes after it restarts, then check_network_status again. Step 7 — APN reset (only if data still won’t improve) • Action: check_apn_settings. If APN/MMSC looks incorrect or blank, reset_apn_settings, then reboot_device once more. Step 8 — SIM reseat (last resort) • Action: reseat_sim_card, then repeat the airplane-mode cycle and check_network_status. Please start with Steps 1–3 now and let me know what network type you see afterward. I’ll adjust immediately based on the new status so we can get you to excellent speed."
}

