  "message": "I’m here to help, and I’ll take this step by step with you. We’ll aim to get you the best possible speed by checking both your phone settings and your account status. Here’s my plan and why: 1) Make sure your phone is actually using mobile data and not being limited by settings like Airplane Mode, Data Saver, VPN, or an older network mode. These are common causes of slow or stopping data. 2) Check your signal and network type (5G/4G). Poor signal or being stuck on older network modes can slow things down. 3) If needed, we’ll reboot to refresh the connection. 4) I’ll also check your line on our side to see if you’ve hit a data limit or need roaming enabled if you’re traveling. Once we do these, we’ll run a quick speed test and compare. I’ll guide you through everything in simple steps. To get started, I need to identify your account so I can also check your line and data usage. Please provide ONE of the following: • Your mobile phone number (best option), or • Your customer ID, or • Your full name AND date of birth (YYYY-MM-DD). A few quick questions so I tailor the steps for you: 1) Are you currently using mobile data or connected to Wi‑Fi? If you’re on Wi‑Fi, please turn Wi‑Fi off temporarily so we test mobile data. 2) Are you traveling outside your usual area or outside the country right now? This helps me check roaming. 3) What kind of phone do you have (iPhone or Android)? 4) Look at the top of your screen (status bar). Do you see: • An airplane icon (Airplane Mode)? • A key icon (VPN)? • “5G”, “4G/LTE”, “3G”, or just signal bars? • Any “Data Saver” icon? Reply with what you see. Once I have your account identified and your answers, I’ll guide you through quick checks (turning off Airplane Mode if on, making sure Mobile Data is ON, turning off Data Saver or VPN if needed, ensuring 4G/5G preferred network mode) and then we’ll check speeds. If the phone-side is all good but speeds aren’t excellent, I’ll check your line for data cap or other account-side limits and fix what I can."
}

