messages.content:
{
  "message": "You’re not doing anything wrong. The “2G” you see is the main reason MMS won’t send. MMS needs at least 3G (ideally 4G/LTE/5G). We’ll switch your phone to prefer faster networks, refresh the connection, and try again.",
  "why_this_helps": "Your line has roaming enabled and extra data added. Now we just need your phone to register on a faster network in France.",
  "steps_on_android": [
    {
      "title": "Set Preferred Network to 4G/5G",
      "steps": [
        "Open Settings.",
        "Tap Network & Internet (or Connections).",
        "Tap Mobile network (or SIMs).",
        "Tap Preferred network type.",
        "Select 5G/4G/3G/2G (Auto) or 4G/5G preferred (anything that includes 4G/LTE or 5G)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Make Sure Network Selection Is Automatic",
      "steps": [
        "Still in Mobile network, tap Network operators (or Carrier).",
        "Turn ON Select network automatically."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Refresh the Connection",
      "steps": [
        "Swipe down from the top twice to open Quick Settings.",
        "Tap the Airplane icon to turn Airplane mode ON.",
        "Wait 15 seconds.",
        "Tap the Airplane icon again to turn it OFF."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Confirm Basics Before Testing",
      "steps": [
        "Keep Wi‑Fi OFF for this test.",
        "Ensure Mobile data is ON and Data roaming is ON (in Mobile network).",
        "Look at the top of the screen: ideally it should say 4G/LTE or 5G. 3G/H/H+ is also OK. If it still shows 2G, move closer to a window or outside for a minute and watch if it changes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Test MMS",
      "steps": [
        "Open Messages.",
        "Open a conversation and attach a photo from your Gallery.",
        "Send the picture while Wi‑Fi is OFF."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "if_still_not_sending": {
    "reason": "Sometimes the APN (which includes the MMS server address) needs a refresh.",
    "steps": [
      "Open Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network.",
      "Tap Access Point Names (APN).",
      "Tap the three dots/menu and choose Reset to default, then confirm.",
      "Restart the phone (hold Power > Restart).",
      "After it restarts, keep Wi‑Fi OFF and try sending the picture again."
    ]
  },
  "reassurance": "You’re doing great. These steps are normal when roaming. Changing these settings won’t delete anything on your phone.",
  "request_update": "Please let me know: after the steps above, what network label do you see (3G/4G/LTE/5G), and did the picture message send? If anything looks different on your screen, tell me exactly what you see and I’ll adjust the steps."
}

