messages.content:
{
  "summary": "Great—your SIM and data connection are now good. The next most likely cause for MMS failures is APN/MMSC configuration or a device setting (Wi‑Fi Calling, Data Saver, VPN, or app permissions). We’ll check and fix those in order.",
  "thought_process": "MMS needs (1) service/data—now confirmed, (2) a correct MMSC URL in APN settings, and (3) no blocking device settings. We’ll verify MMSC first because a missing/incorrect MMSC is a very common MMS blocker, especially when roaming.",
  "steps_in_order": [
    {
      "step": "Check APN/MMSC settings",
      "why": "MMS will fail if the MMSC URL is missing or wrong.",
      "how": [
        "Run check_apn_settings on your phone.",
        "Tell me: the APN name and whether the MMSC URL is present (not blank)."
      ],
      "if_mmsc_missing_or_incorrect": [
        "Run reset_apn_settings to restore the default carrier APN.",
        "Then run reboot_device to apply changes.",
        "After reboot, keep Wi‑Fi OFF, Mobile Data ON, Data Roaming ON, and try sending an MMS to yourself."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Check Wi‑Fi Calling status",
      "why": "In some configurations, Wi‑Fi Calling can interfere with MMS.",
      "how": [
        "Run check_wifi_calling_status.",
        "If it shows ON, run toggle_wifi_calling to turn it OFF.",
        "Retry sending an MMS to yourself."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Confirm Data Saver is OFF",
      "why": "Data Saver can restrict background data that MMS relies on.",
      "how": [
        "Run check_data_restriction_status.",
        "If Data Saver is ON, run toggle_data_saver_mode to turn it OFF.",
        "Retry MMS."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Ensure no VPN is active",
      "why": "A VPN can sometimes break MMS routing.",
      "how": [
        "Run check_vpn_status.",
        "If a VPN is connected, run disconnect_vpn.",
        "Retry MMS."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Verify messaging app permissions",
      "why": "The app needs Storage and SMS permissions to send/receive MMS.",
      "how": [
        "Run check_app_permissions with app_name=\"messaging\".",
        "If Storage or SMS isn’t granted, run grant_app_permission for each missing one.",
        "Retry MMS."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "what_to_do_now": [
    "Please start with Step 1 (APN/MMSC). Run check_apn_settings and share the APN name and whether the MMSC URL is present. If the MMSC is missing/blank, go ahead and reset_apn_settings, then reboot_device, and test an MMS to yourself."
  ],
  "ask_for_update": "What does check_apn_settings show for the MMSC URL? If you reset and rebooted, did the MMS to yourself send successfully?"
}

