messages.content:
{
  "thought_process": "After toggling Airplane Mode, phones sometimes take a moment to re-register on the network, and mobile data can also remain OFF. Since you’re seeing “No Signal” and “Data Disabled,” we’ll first make sure Airplane Mode is truly OFF and Mobile Data is ON, then verify the SIM and network settings. This targets the most likely causes in the right order.",
  "steps_now": [
    {
      "title": "Confirm Airplane Mode is OFF",
      "why": "If Airplane Mode stayed ON, you’ll have no signal.",
      "how_android": "Open Quick Settings and ensure the Airplane icon is NOT highlighted. If it is, tap to turn it OFF. Wait 30–60 seconds to see if signal bars return."
    },
    {
      "title": "Turn Mobile Data ON",
      "why": "You’re seeing “Data Disabled”; MMS and browsing need mobile data.",
      "how_android": "In Quick Settings, make sure the Mobile Data icon is ON. If it’s OFF, tap to enable it. Wait ~10 seconds and check if the signal/data icons appear."
    },
    {
      "title": "Check SIM status",
      "why": "If the SIM is missing/locked, the phone can’t register to the network.",
      "how_android": "Settings > Network & Internet > SIMs (or About phone > SIM status). Please tell me what it shows: Active, Missing, or Locked."
    }
  ],
  "if_results": [
    {
      "condition": "SIM shows Missing",
      "do": "Reseat the SIM (this simulates removing/reinserting): Settings path may vary, but use the SIM/eSIM settings to reseat if available, or power off and physically reseat if it’s a physical SIM. Then power back on and wait 1 minute."
    },
    {
      "condition": "SIM shows Locked",
      "do": "Do not guess PIN/PUK. Tell me right away and I’ll transfer you to a human agent for SIM security assistance."
    },
    {
      "condition": "SIM shows Active but still No Signal",
      "do": [
        "Set preferred network to 4G/5G: Settings > Network & Internet > Mobile network > Preferred network type > choose 5G/4G/3G (auto).",
        "Reboot the phone to refresh the radio registration.",
        "After reboot, ensure Mobile Data is ON, then try sending the MMS again."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "ask_to_report_back": [
    "Is Airplane Mode OFF now?",
    "Were you able to turn Mobile Data ON?",
    "What does the SIM status say (Active/Missing/Locked)?",
    "After these steps, did your signal bars return and can you send the MMS?"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "If the network just needed to re-register, signal should come back within a minute after Airplane Mode is OFF.",
    "If we confirm SIM is Active and settings are correct but you still have no signal, we’ll proceed to additional checks. I’ll stay with you step-by-step."
  ]
}

