messages.content:
{
  "thought_process": "I looked up your line ending in 2002. It’s Active, international roaming is enabled on our side, and you’ve used 8.7 GB out of 15 GB this cycle (so you still have data). Since you’re in France, MMS needs mobile data and Data Roaming ON on the phone itself. The most likely causes now are: data/roaming toggles OFF on the phone, Wi‑Fi Calling/VPN/Data Saver interfering, network mode stuck on 2G, or APN/MMSC settings needing a reset.",
  "plan": "We’ll do quick phone-side checks in order: ensure mobile data and data roaming are ON, turn off Wi‑Fi Calling, verify network mode (4G/5G), briefly toggle data, test mobile web, then reset APN if needed and reboot. After each step, try sending an MMS.",
